ce070" position="anchor" mimetype="application" mime-subtype="pdf"/></supplementary-material><supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="SD5"><label>File S5</label><caption><p>Majority rule consensus trees with bootstrap support for Tctex1/2 sequences, as inferred using Bayesian, ML, NJ and MP approaches (see Materials and Methods).</p></caption><media xlink:href="tra0008-1708_8_12dfig5.pdf" xlink:type="simple" id="N0x1c415d0N0x31ce130" position="anchor" mimetype="application" mime-subtype="pdf"/></supplementary-material><supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="SD6"><label>File S6</label><caption><p>Classification of the divergent Chlamydomonas dynein 206178. Tree shown is the consensus of 10 Bayesian tree inference runs with character resampling. Topology support from Bayesian, ML, NJ and MP approaches is shown next to selected nodes.</p></caption><media xlink:href="tra0008-1708_8_12dfig6.pdf" xlink:type="simple" id="N0x1c415d0N0x31ce1f0" position="anchor" mimetype="application" mime-subtype="pdf"/></supplementary-material><supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="SD7"><label>File S7</label><caption><p>Histogram showing the distribution of scores for all sequences encoded 24 diverse eukaryotes, queried with a HMM built from an alignment of dynein IC sequences.</p></caption><media xlink:href="tra0008-1708_8_12dfig7.pdf" xlink:type="simple" id="N0x1c415d0N0x31ce2b0" position="anchor" mimetype="application" mime-subtype="pdf"/></supplementary-material><supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="SD8"><label>File S8</label><caption><p>Reciprocal-best-BLAST hits from 24 diverse eukaryotes, queried with sequences identified in Chlamydomonas as OAD docking complex components, dynein ICs, proteins involved inIFT, dynein LCs, dynein LICs and radial spoke proteins and also components of the human cytoplasmic dynein 1 complex.</p></caption><media xlink:href="tra0008-1708_8_12dfig8.xls" xlink:type="simple" id="N0x1c415d0N0x31ce370" p